HST Office: a push button's label stays readable on the coat's fill (WCAG AA) in every state, light and dark,
on every platform: the Save button of the "Save Document?" dialog had white text on a near-white fill on macOS.

- The coat fills every push button with the light (dark) control colour and marks a default button by its
  accent border only, but the label is drawn by PushButton in the colour the platform chose for its own bezel.
  macOS (vcl/osx/salframe.cxx) gives a default button alternateSelectedControlTextColor (white) because its
  native default bezel is the accent: white on #F5F8FC (1.05:1). Before Big Sur it does the same for a
  pressed button.
- hst::coat::ReadablePushButtonText (coat-buttons.cxx): where the coat draws, the platform's label colour is
  kept when it reads (4.5:1) on the coat's fill for the state (resting, hover, pressed) and replaced by the
  palette's text colour otherwise; one call in PushButton::ImplDrawPushButtonContent, not for buttons with
  their own foreground or background colour. No colour, shape or size of the coat changes.
- gtk3: a default button's label (not a primary action's, which keeps the accent and its ink) takes the
  palette's text colour, so a theme's light label for its own coloured default fill cannot vanish on the
  coat's fill.
- Test: CoatTest::testPushButtonLabelReadable.
